# Copy to .env and fill in. Only the API key belongs in this file.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-...

# Optional overrides (these are the defaults)
# Any vision model works. Measured against the labelled set in bench/, models around
# $0.03-$0.06 per million tokens produce the same verdicts as ones costing 40x more.
# TC_MODEL=google/gemini-3.8-flash
# TC_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# TC_HOST=127.0.0.1
# TC_PORT=8787
# TC_DAILY_LIMIT=40
# TC_ENV_FILE=/path/to/.env
# TC_SIGNING_KEY=/path/to/key.pem

# The daily limit counts per client address. A proxy header is set by the client, so it is only the
# caller when something in front overwrote it. Left unset, it is trusted when the connection comes
# from a non-public address - a tunnel or reverse proxy next to the app, which is how a self-hosted
# instance is published - so each visitor gets their own allowance instead of everyone sharing one.
# Set 1 to always trust it (a CDN that connects from public addresses, where the origin must not be
# reachable without going through it), or 0 to never trust it and key on the socket address.
# TC_TRUST_PROXY=

# The instance-wide spend ceiling. The key's own limit at the provider is the backstop that cannot be
# bypassed; this is the app's own guard, read from the provider where possible and from a local ledger
# otherwise. A cached report costs nothing and is served even when the budget is spent.
# TC_BUDGET_USD=5
# TC_BUDGET_FILE=/path/to/budget.json
# TC_BUDGET_TTL_MS=60000

# Visitors may bring their own key, and may name their own endpoint. An endpoint is only accepted
# together with a visitor's key (never the deployment's), and is refused if it points anywhere
# private. Set to 0 to refuse visitor-supplied endpoints entirely.
# TC_ALLOW_CUSTOM_ENDPOINT=1

# Reports keep the submitted photos, and that is not optional: a permalink has to show the picture
# its verdict was reached from. Each is served only while it still hashes to the digest the report
# carries, so the image on the page is provably the one that was analysed.
# TC_PHOTO_BUDGET_MB caps the stored photos (oldest first). Off by default; setting it means a
# report can outlive its pictures, which is a deliberate trade rather than the default.
# TC_PHOTO_BUDGET_MB=2048
